Contour cards lit like iOS Liquid Glass.

- The bevel line lights the edges facing the light and the ones facing away
  (both surfaces of a pane reflect it) and fades on the edges parallel to it:
  with the light at the top, a line along the top and bottom and none on the
  sides. On the reference the left and right rims are invisible.
- No inner bottom shadow on traced cards: the reference cards are lifted and
  light, never sunk.
- The two lines are kept equally bright whatever the layer's shape: a line
  along the layer box's own edge is clipped by it and keeps ~0.41 of its core
  (a toast touching its layer's top, a bar that fills its layer), so it gets
  1.58 where a line with room beyond it gets 0.65; and the lit side, which the
  specular highlight already brightens, is weighted down to 0.63 of the far
  side. Measured on Noctalia's toast (top clipped) and bar (both clipped).

